{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q016_pdb_1acc_domain_split","answer":"SCOP 1.75 represented chain A as one whole-chain domain, d1acca_ (SUNID 43828; SCCS f.11.1.1), in the class-f “Anthrax protective antigen” fold, superfamily, and family. This remained unchanged through SCOPe 2.03. Beginning with SCOPe 2.04, and still in the current stable release 2.08, it was replaced by two domains: d1acca2 (SUNID 238522), residues A:14–225, is b.179.1.1—class b (all-beta), Anthrax protective antigen N-terminal-like fold, PA14-like superfamily, PA14 family; d1acca1 (SUNID 238521), residues A:226–735, is f.60.1.1—class f, Anthrax protective antigen C-terminal-like fold, superfamily, and family. Thus the old f.11 classification should not be propagated to either modern domain.

The revision shows that a polypeptide chain is not necessarily one evolutionary unit: 1accA contains separately delimited modules assigned even to different structural classes and folds, consistent with distinct evolutionary histories and possible domain fusion or shuffling. Their coexistence in protective antigen does not establish homology between the two modules. Family membership supports close homology, superfamily membership supports more remote common ancestry, while a fold- or class-level resemblance alone is not sufficient evidence of homology or shared function.

Homology searches should therefore use residues 14–225 and 226–735 as separate sequence and structure queries, inspect matches and alignments per domain, and use domain-specific templates. A match to PA14-like d1acca2 supports ancestry only for the N-terminal module; a match to d1acca1 supports only the C-terminal module. Neither licenses transfer of whole-protein function, domain architecture, binding specificity, or the unmatched region, and a template covering one domain should not be extrapolated across the other. Full-chain searches may still identify proteins sharing the complete architecture, but can conceal a weaker one-domain relationship or let the longer C-terminal region dominate the score.","evidence_used":["/api/v1/","/api/v1/releases/1.75/pdb/1acc","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1acc","/api/v1/releases/1.75/pdb/1acc/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1acc/domains","/api/v1/releases/1.75/resolve/d1acca_","/api/v1/releases/2.08/resolve/d1acca1","/api/v1/releases/2.08/resolve/d1acca2","/api/v1/releases/1.75/sunids/43828","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/238521","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/238522","/api/v1/releases/1.75/sunids/56991","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/254762","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/254763","/api/v1/releases/1.75/sunids/56990","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/254333","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/254334","/api/v1/releases/1.75/sunids/56989","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/254146","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/254147","/api/v1/releases/1.75/sunids/56988","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/254122","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/254123","/api/v1/releases/1.75/sunids/56987","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/254103","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/254104","/api/v1/releases","/api/v1/releases/2.01/pdb/1acc/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.02/pdb/1acc/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.03/pdb/1acc/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.04/pdb/1acc/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.05/pdb/1acc/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.06/pdb/1acc/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.07/pdb/1acc/domains"]}]}
